cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use XPOSim in your research, please cite this software using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "XPOSim: X-ray Paraxial Optical Simulation"
authors:
  - family-names: Aleksandrov
    given-names: Aleksandr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6131-6088"
version: "0.38.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mamichberdey/XPOSim"
url: "https://github.com/mamichberdey/XPOSim"
abstract: >-
  XPOSim is a Python library for scalar paraxial X-ray wave propagation,
  diffraction and focusing on one- and two-dimensional grids, with NumPy,
  CuPy, PyTorch and JAX numerical backends.
keywords:
  - X-ray optics
  - wave optics
  - Fresnel diffraction
  - compound refractive lenses
  - scientific computing
